  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Unity.TextMeshPro::TMPro.TextMeshProUGUI
  m_Material: {fileID: 0}
  m_Color: {r: 1, g: 1, b: 1, a: 1}
  m_RaycastTarget: 1
  m_RaycastPadding: {x: 0, y: 0, z: 0, w: 0}
  m_Maskable: 1
  m_OnCullStateChanged:
    m_PersistentCalls:
      m_Calls: []
  m_text: 'If a player goes bankrupt owing money to another player, ownership of all the bankrupt player''s properties transfer over to the player that is owed money. Any mortgaged properties will remain mortgaged until the new owner pays the original mortgage +10% interest to the bank.


    As you move around the board, you will find additional spaces aside from properties that can help or hinder your goal of becoming the wealthiest player:


    Chance and Community


    Chest If you land on one of these spaces, you receive a card from the appropriate deck and automatically follow the instructions.


    Tax Spaces


    If you land on the Luxury Tax space, pay $I00. The Income Tax space will charge you $200.


    Free Parking


    Free Parking is just a free resting place. You receive no money for landing on this space unless you alter the House Rules. Keep in mind that adding more money to the game can extend the duration of the session.


    GO


    As you pass GO, you collect a salary. This is $200 by default, but can be customized in House Rules.


    Jail


    You can be sent directly to Jail by landing on the "Go to Jail" space. Rolling doubles three times in a row will send you to Jail. When in Jail, you can pay bail, roll for doubles to get out free, or use a I''Get Out of Jail Free" card.'
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
  m_fontAsset: {fileID: 11400000, guid: a4fa899acf0f401448e55d200f2bc407, type: 2}
